<title>SINGAPORE: India cancels tender to buy Dec 96-Mar 97 fuel oil.</title>
<headline>India cancels tender to buy Dec 96-Mar 97 fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has cancelled its tender to buy 3.5-percent sulphur fuel oil for deliveries between December and March 1997, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>IOC had given no reasons for cancelling the tender, they said.</p>
<p>IOC had sought 45,000 tonnes each month of 180-centistoke grade fuel oil for deliveries to Kandla and Bombay on the Indian west coast.</p>
<p>The tender was scheduled to close on November 20 for one-day validity.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (+65-870 3082)</p>
